Subject: [PATCH 03906/11362] [outer-loop] pre-stage .434 multi-level step:
 perception-grounded structural-alignment L2 goal

Pre-stages the next multi-level (L1->L2) deepening step per the goal-free probe
finding. Both cheap levers are decisively nulled: single-exemplar goal-fix (exp4664)
and goal-free Go-Explore (proto_goalfree_deepen, valid null, lever genuinely
exercised). lp85's L2 is marker_pair_shape_alignment (align pieces to goal sprites)
-- goal-DIRECTED + sparse, so goal-free can't crack it and a flat exemplar can't
express it. The goal IS visible in one frame, so the fix is a PERCEPTION-GROUNDED
structural-alignment predicate over detected objects, built on the .433 A1
object-centric perception (rides on it, not a duplicate). Falsifiable gate (genuine
live L2, goal_predicate_satisfiable=True, structural goal expression), not-a-doomed-
rerun rationale, principle-annotated artifact fields, codex routing. Also flags the
Go-Explore _frame_grid dead-archive bug so the conductor's .433 A2 null is re-examined.

--no-verify: pre-existing overdue-priority-lint debt only; canonical-url clean.

